# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#1173, pipenv creates a %userprofile%\.virtualenvs folder
#   So you don't need to ignore a local .venv folder if you use it in its default mode.
#   But if you set PIPENV_VENV_IN_PROJECT=1, it creates a .venv directory in the project
#   For that, see the global "environments" section above.
